$CATEGORY: Q13 - Random numbers

::Q1301::
nondeterministic {
    =A program that does the same thing every time it is run.
    =A program that behaves differently even when run multiple times with the same input
}

::Q1302::
pseudorandom - A sequence of numbers that appear to be random but are actually the product of a deterministic computation. {TRUE}

$CATEGORY: Q12 - Arrays and strings

::Q1201::
array - a collection of values in which all the values have the same type. {TRUE}

::Q1202::
element - One of the values in an array. The [] operator selects elements. {TRUE}

::Q1203::
index - an integer variable or value used to indicate an element of an array. {TRUE}

::Q1204::
allocate - to reserve memory for an array or other object. In Java, the new operator allocates memory. {TRUE}

::Q1205::
reference - a value that indicates a storage location. In a memory diagram, a reference appears as an arrow. {TRUE}

::Q1206::
alias - a variable that refers to the same object as another variable. {TRUE}

::Q1207::
traversal - looping through the elements of an array (or other collection). {TRUE}

::Q1208::
search - a traversal pattern used to find a particular element of an array. {TRUE}

::Q1209::
reduce - a traversal pattern that combines the elements of an array into a single value.{TRUE}

::Q1210::
accumulator - a variable used to accumulate results during a traversal. {TRUE}

::Q1211::
histogram - an array of integers in which each integer counts the number of values that fall into a certain range.{TRUE}

::Q1212::
enhanced for loop - an alternative syntax for traversing the elements of an array (or other collection). {TRUE}